  Id: hd110067_star
  DisplayName: HD 110067
  Subtitle: THE HOST STAR
  Paragraph: A K-type dwarf a little cooler and smaller than the Sun, in Coma Berenices, about 105 light years away. It is bright enough to keep studying, and old - somewhere around seven to eight billion years. From any of its six planets it would look like a warm white disc several times wider than the Sun looks from Earth.
